 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“It is important for us my brothers that we exterminate from our land this nation which only seeks to kill us. . . . When I go to the English chief to tell him that some of our comrades are dead . . . he makes fun of me and you. When I ask him for something for our sick, he refuses, and tells me he has no need of us. You can well see by that that he seeks our ruin. . . . There is no more time to lose, and when the English shall be defeated . . . we shall cut off the passage so that they cannot come back to our country.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">Pontiac, Ottawa Chief, May 1763</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 614947,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "One important consequence of the belief expressed in the excerpt was",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167760,
     "content_html": "slaves from the colonies escaped to Maroon Communities in the West"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167761,
     "content_html": "American Indian tribes allied with each other to try to defeat the British"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167759,
     "content_html": "women came to the defense of Pontiac and donated family money to his cause"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167758,
     "content_html": "negotiations were opened with Colonists and violent conflict was avoided"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 614948,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The sentiments expressed in the excerpt provided most directly caused which of the following events?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167764,
     "content_html": "The American Revolution was fought shortly thereafter against the American Indian tribes in the Ohio River Valley."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167763,
     "content_html": "The French and Indian War was fought in competition for the territory west of the Mississippi."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167765,
     "content_html": "An uprising of American Indians challenged British frontier forces and resulted in concessions that angered the colonists."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167762,
     "content_html": "King Philip’s War was fought in New England to resist the encroachment and cruelty of British colonists."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 614949,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which of the following events in U.S. history is most similar to the excerpt provided?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167768,
     "content_html": "Vesey’s Rebellion pitted free and enslaved peoples against white families in a southern city."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167767,
     "content_html": "The Bread Riots highlighted the lack of supplies during war available to families and created chaos and violence."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167769,
     "content_html": "The Battle of Tippecanoe pitted U.S. citizens against the Shawnee tribe over the Indiana territory."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167766,
     "content_html": "The Seneca Falls Convention promoted the rights of women despite an oppressive society."
    }
   ],
